# Execute agreed plans without reconfirmation

When the user says they like a plan, "do all of those", "follow your gut", or similar:

- Implement the full plan in the same session — fixes, launches, config patches, eval reruns, fleet changes.
- Do not end turns with "want me to…?" for steps already covered by the approved plan.
- Only stop to ask when blocked on a genuine fork (missing data, destructive action outside the plan, or conflicting user constraints).

Brief status updates are fine; permission-seeking for every sub-step is not.
